course: dictionary
lesson: 5256
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the dictionary gives each one a number. Joker is a good example: it can be a person, a playing card, or an unkind name for someone annoying. «The class joker made everyone laugh during the spelling test.» The words class and laugh are your clues, so here a joker is a person who likes to make jokes.
explain: Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning. «A scientist was sure that a joker had sewn a duck's bill onto a furry animal.» Sewing and a trick tell you this joker is a person playing a practical joke. Always ask: what is the topic of this sentence? People, games, or school?
explain: Some meanings are informal, which means they are used in everyday talk, not in formal writing. «Jokes about someone's family are bullying, and the one being unkind is the joker.» Here joker is an unkind name, so it is not a compliment. Check your choice by swapping in your meaning and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A joker is a person who likes to make jokes and do funny things.
fact: The joker is a playing card with a picture of a jester, and in some games it can stand for any other card.
fact: A joker can also be an annoying or silly person; this meaning is informal and unkind.
fact: Useful phrases: the class joker, a practical joker, joker in the pack.
fact: A kind joke makes people laugh together; a joke that only the joker enjoys is picking on someone.
exercise: «The class joker made everyone laugh during the spelling test.» What is a joker here? | *A person who likes to make jokes | A tool for cutting paper | A playing card with a jester | A kind of bird
exercise: In some card games, what can the joker stand for? | Only the number one | The final score of the game | *Any other card | The name of the dealer
exercise: Which meaning of joker is informal and unkind? | A jester in a king's court | *An annoying or silly person | Someone who likes to make jokes | A playing card
test: «Mia dealt the cards, and the joker was face up on top.» What is the joker in this sentence? | An annoying person | A toy made from bits of two others | A person who tells jokes | *A playing card with a picture of a jester
test: «Jokes about someone's family are bullying, and the one being unkind is the joker.» What does joker mean in this sentence? | A kind of sloth in a cartoon | A playing card | *An unkind person who picks on others | A friendly person who makes everyone laugh
exam: «Leo's practical joker friend hid the teacher's chalk, and nobody thought it was funny.» What does practical joker suggest? | Someone who is always tired and slow | A person who sells playing cards | *Someone who plays tricks on people | A kind helper in the class
